.fi
Nokizaru is a CLI tool purpose-built for enumerating the core web recon surface.
It can collect common recon signals from a target such as HTTP headers,
SSL/TLS certificate details, WHOIS, DNS records, subdomains, architecture
fingerprinting, crawler link extraction, directory enumeration, Wayback URLs,
and also features a fast port scan.
.SH SCAN TARGET
The target is required for scans, but not for help, version output, or saving
an API key.
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
OPTION	MEANING
--target TARGET	Target (http[s]://host[:port])
.TE
.SH MODULE SELECTION OPTIONS
These options enable modules. You may enable multiple in one run.
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
OPTION	MODULE
--headers	Header Information
--sslinfo	SSL Certificate Information
--whois	Whois Lookup
--crawl	Crawl Target
--dns	DNS Enumeration
--sub	Sub-Domain Enumeration
--arch	Architecture Fingerprinting
--dir	Directory Search
--wayback	Wayback URLs
--ps	Fast Port Scan
--full	Full Recon
--no-[MODULE]	Skip specified modules above during full scan (e.g. --no-dir)
--export	Write results to export directory
.TE
.SH EXTRA OPTIONS
.TS
box, allbox;
l l l.
OPTION	MEANING	DEFAULT / NOTES
-h, --help	Show help and exit	-
-v, --version	Show version number and exit	-
-nb	Hide Banner	-
-dt DT	Directory enum threads	50
-pt PT	Port scan concurrency	50
-p PORTS	Port scan ports	Curated top 100+ ports
-T T	Base timeout / module budget (seconds)	30.0
-w W	Wordlist size (small, medium, large) or custom path	medium
-H, --header HEADER	Add custom request header (repeatable)	Example: Cookie: PHPSESSID=abc
-r	Follow redirects during directory enum	False
-s	Enable SSL verification for directory enum	False
-sp SP	Specify SSL port	443
-d D	Custom DNS servers	8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4,1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1
-e E	File extension(s) (comma separated)	Example: txt,xml,php
-o O	Export Format(s) (comma-separated)	txt,json,html
-cd CD	Export directory for this run (requires --export)	XDG data dir/nokizaru/dumps/nk_<hostname>
-of OF	Export filename base for this run (requires --export)	YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS
-k K	Add API key (NAME@KEY)	shodan@key
.TE
.SH API KEYS
Some providers require API keys. Missing credentials skip only that provider;
architecture fingerprinting is skipped entirely without a Wappalyzer key.
Keys may be provided via environment variables (NK_*) or saved under the XDG
data directory.
.PP
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
ENV VAR	PROVIDER
NK_BEVIGIL_KEY	BeVigil
NK_BINEDGE_KEY	BinaryEdge
NK_CENSYS_API_ID	Censys API ID
NK_CENSYS_API_SECRET	Censys API Secret
NK_CHAOS_KEY	Chaos
NK_FB_KEY	Facebook
NK_HUNTER_KEY	Hunter
NK_NETLAS_KEY	Netlas
NK_SHODAN_KEY	Shodan
NK_VT_KEY	VirusTotal
NK_WAPPALYZER_KEY	Wappalyzer
NK_ZOOMEYE_KEY	ZoomEye
.TE
.PP
To add a key from the CLI:
.PP
.nf
nokizaru -k shodan@YOURKEY
.fi
.SH FILES
Paths honor XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME. The defaults are shown below.
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
PATH	PURPOSE
$HOME/.config/nokizaru/config.json	Main configuration file
$HOME/.local/share/nokizaru/keys.json	API keys file (optional)
$HOME/.local/share/nokizaru/dumps/	Export directory for run outputs
$HOME/.local/share/nokizaru/nokizaru.log	Runtime log file
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
COMMAND	DESCRIPTION
nokizaru --full --target https://example.com	Full recon
nokizaru --headers --target https://example.com	Header inspection
nokizaru --arch --target https://example.com	Architecture fingerprinting
nokizaru --dir --target https://example.com -e php,xml	Directory enum with extensions
nokizaru --crawl --dir --target https://example.com -H 'Cookie: PHPSESSID=abc; uid=52'	Authenticated in-scope scan
nokizaru --wayback --target https://example.com	Wayback URLs
nokizaru --ps --target https://example.com -pt 80	Port scan with higher concurrency
nokizaru --ps --target https://example.com -p all	Port scan all TCP ports
.TE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TS
box, allbox;
l l.
CODE	MEANING
0	Run completed; individual modules may be failed or skipped
1	Failure (invalid target, missing target, runtime error)
130	Interrupted (Ctrl-C)
143	Terminated (SIGTERM)
.TE
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Run ONLY against targets you have explicit permission to test.
Nokizaru is intended for authorized security testing ONLY.
